+**Macindoe adjudication record (2026-07-30) — the round-12 Rhin 13.3 re-source warning.** No script needed (a literature adjudication on this entry's ingredient; nothing here needed computing). **Grade (a): 13.3 CONFIRMED for exactly what this chain consumes.** The primary statement is Rhin 1987 (Progress in Mathematics 71, Proposition p. 160): for all integers `u₀, u₁, u₂` with `H = max(|u₁|,|u₂|)`, `|u₀ + u₁·log 2 + u₂·log 3| > H^(−13.3)` — a linear-form bound covering `(log 2, log 3)` directly, confirmed by four printed carriers: Simons–de Weger 2005 (Acta Arith. 117, Lemma 12: `Λ > e^(−13.3(0.46057+log K))`, proof "We apply the Proposition on p. 160 of [Rh]..."; their own sourcing sentence: "for our specific case x log 2 + y log 3 however, the result of Rhin [Rh] is best"); an independent generalized-Collatz application (arXiv:2205.10582, Lemmas 10/12, both height cases exercised); the zbMATH review of the paper (Zbl 0632.10034: it proves both irrationality measures of single numbers **and** "une très bonne mesure d'indépendance linéaire sur ℤ effective de 1, log 2 et log 3"); and Wu 2003 (Math. Comp. 72, p. 902: Rhin's own linear independence measure of `1, log 2, log 3` at 7.616, cited as the source of the best-known `μ(log 3) ≤ 8.616`). Merle's own `BILAN_R201.md` (`Collatz-Junction-Theorem`, commit `6d30395`) is wrong on its stated premise ("Rhin (1987) traite des mesures d'irrationalité de log 2, pas des formes linéaires en 2 logarithmes") — the paper proves both — and its replacement constants (Laurent 2008 ≈18.5, LMN 1995 ≈23.55) are coefficients of a different instrument, a `(log)²`-shaped bound, not exponents on the height. Its trigger was nonetheless real: R200's own transcription had written Rhin's constant into that `(log)²` shape (`exp(−13.3·(log S)²)`), which is genuinely not Rhin's; the auditor rejected the attribution where the actual defect was the transcription. No number in this entry moves — the headline `< 5.2·10⁻⁴` beyond `n ≈ 2233` and every committed threshold stand unmoved, and the source line needs no edit. The one boundary this session leaves exactly where round 9 and round 10 left it: Rhin's printed hypotheses on p. 160 (any threshold `H₀`) remain unread from the 1987 volume (paywalled); both published applications above apply it thresholdless from moderate heights, and this entry's use needs only `H = K₀ ≥ 952`. Record: `briefs/merle-la7-rhin-check-findings.md`.
 
